--------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Purpose & Architecture
--------------------------------------------------------------------

NoteSpaceLLM is a local-first PySide6 desktop application for document analysis,
research, and report generation across PDF, Word (DOCX), Markdown, plain text,
spreadsheets (XLSX), and email archives (EML, MSG). Project files and the
ChromaDB index are stored locally by default. When a remote model or embedding
endpoint is configured, the text and prompts used for that operation are sent
to the selected endpoint. A lightweight Web/PWA Companion opens exported
workspaces in a browser.

The following are selected implementation notes for this source snapshot, not a
security certification, complete network audit, complete SBOM, or legal
compliance assessment:
  * The app disables ChromaDB's anonymized telemetry for its local client and
    does not implement its own telemetry. This does not characterize behavior
    of the operating system, browser, extensions, or configured providers.
  * Saved credential fields are excluded from workspace exports, but user-authored
    reports and chats may contain secrets and should be checked before sharing.
  * A remote Ollama endpoint receives document text used for embeddings and
    prompts/context for responses. An API key is sent to the configured URL in
    a Bearer header; HTTP does not encrypt content or credentials.
  * The PWA service worker caches application shell assets. Imported workspace
    content is kept in the current page session and is not cached as workspace
    data by the app.
  * Declared dependency version constraints and selected license notes are
    listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt. They are
    not a resolved dependency inventory, security audit, or compatibility review.

